# `given name: T = expr` has no members to reach — REFUSED

No `.expected`, so the front gate requires this to be refused.

G1 supports exactly one spelling: `given name: T with` and a block of members. An instance written
as a VALUE has nothing to flatten into an object, and accepting it would mean deciding what
`intMonoid.combine` resolves to — which is the type-directed question G1 explicitly does not answer
(`v3/SPRINT.md` SSC3-G2).

Refused BY NAME rather than parsed into something plausible: before `given` was claimed at all, this
line reached the parser as two expressions and stopped at the `:` with `expected an expression`, a
message that names the punctuation instead of the construct.

```scalascript
trait Monoid:
  def empty: Int

given intMonoid: Monoid = Monoid()

println("unreachable")
```
